WEBVTT

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.490
Good work.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.330
You, too. See you tomorrow.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.360
Yeah.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.020
That reminds me...

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.100
You're looking well, Aoyama.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.910
Kurata Kozue, what are you doing in Japan?

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.010
I wonder who that woman was.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:38.510
Who knows? Aoyama never talks about himself.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:43.850
We don't know anything about him,
not even where he lives.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.770
I guess he's being extremely secretive
in order to keep his distance from people.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:52.030
Aoyama-kun, good work!

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.870
It looks like Aoyama has 
more than just one secret.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.040
<b>#10</b>

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.040
<b>Aoyama-kun Has Many Secrets</b>

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.710
All right, there he goes.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.130
Let's go!

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.620
Team Discover Aoyama's Secrets: move out!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.050
<b>This work is a piece of fiction. 
Please do not ride bikes like this!</b>

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.570
Just so we're clear...

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:48.310
I'm only coming along because I'm worried 
you three will get up to mischief.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:51.130
It's not like I want to
know more about Aoyama.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:52.810
Sure, sure.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.610
We'll be done for the day once 
we found out where Aoyama lives.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:00.320
Don't fall behind, Unit 2!

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.970
Go! Go! Go!

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.660
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.310
This is totally unfair!

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:15.040
<b>And definitely do <i>not</i> ride 
in this pathetic manner!</b>

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.660
It's your fault for losing 
at rock, paper, scissors.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.100
If you have the breath to complain,
pedal harder!

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.590
Dammit!

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.050
But I'm really interested to 
know where Aoyama lives.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:28.050
I picture him living in some model room
for a high-rise apartment block.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.810
Something that doesn't feel homely at all.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.940
Nah, I think his place will be more like 
a mansion, with a butler and the works.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.820
I can see him gazing at a photo
of his daddy and sister in his room

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:43.230
and saying "good night" to it
before he goes to sleep.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.060
Are you guys talking about my place?!
 How the hell do you even know that?!

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.410
What? You seriously do all that?

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.830
Huh? Where did Aoyama go?

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.750
It's absolutely packed here.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.840
Well, this <i>is</i> the shopping district.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:05.090
There! He got off his bike and 
he's walking through the crowd!

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.970
Whoa, he's fast!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.850
He's moving so fast that everyone else
looks like they're standing still!

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.440
Has he realized we're tailing him?!

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.600
Don't lose him!

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.940
Excuse me, miss!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.600
Oh, sorry!

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:20.990
This meat's so good.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.490
Don't make yourself even heavier!

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.310
There he is! It's Aoyama!

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.990
He's already all the way over there!

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.390
He jumped?!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.750
<b>Kids at home: 
Do <i>not</i> copy Aoyama!</b>

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.220
No way.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.760
Is he for real?!

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.430
He survived that?!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.010
That monster.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.140
Is he telling us not to follow him?

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.450
But why is he going to such lengths 
to keep things about him concealed?

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.900
Maybe his home is his safe space?

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:14.540
He wants to maintain a clean state,
leaving no information about him behind.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.850
He doesn't want anybody 
to enter his personal space.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:22.670
Well, it does sound like him, but even so...

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.490
We've come this far! 
We can't retreat now!

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.800
Zaizen!

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.060
<b>Kids at home:
 Do <i>not</i> copy Zaizen!</b>

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.670
Are you stupid, Zaizen? 
There are stairs right here!

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.450
Can you give me a hand? I can't get up.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.820
You deserve that for getting
carried away and jumping!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:56.830
Just don't do anything they're doing!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.330
It's been quite a while 
since we lost sight of him.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.840
He might already be home.

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:09.840
You want to go in that store over there?

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:14.270
I'm hungry, so why not? Zaizen's treat.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:15.850
Looks like I'll have to.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:22.980
Aoyama!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.310
That's too much food for just himself.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.740
It's enough to feed a family.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:36.700
That means...

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:38.850
<i>...the goal is in sight!</i>

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.630
<i>Is that it?</i>

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.220
Huh?

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:02.800
Is this Aoyama's house?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.180
It's nothing like we imagined.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.230
Well, then...

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:11.230
As if Aoyama would 
ever let us in if we asked!

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.380
We're storming the place!

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.990
Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.130
Aoyama!

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:30.010
Y-You're...

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.370
Ibuki Seigo?!

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:37.510
I heard you signed with the youth team
of a renowned Spanish club!

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.530
What are you doing in Aoyama's house?!

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.520
No, this is my place.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.570
Then why is Aoyama here making food?!

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:50.180
Because I beat him in a match.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:07.540
Thanks for the food.

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:17.060
So good, so good.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:24.060
You lost? I can't believe it.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:28.760
He's been cooking for himself since he began
making the age-group national teams.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:31.070
We've been wagering
home-cooked meals ever since,

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.990
and I've always eating his food like this.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.390
But you've really improved.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:40.080
One slip-up,

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.630
and I wouldn't have been able to eat 
today's chicken-and-egg rice bowl.

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:56.670
<i>They're going to have another match?</i>

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.430
<i>Oh, yeah. Where is Aoyama's house?</i>

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.490
<i>Save it for another day...</i>

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.110
<b>Ibuki Seigo</b>

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.110
<b>National Youth 
Superstar!</b>

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.110
<b>Earnest Childhood Friend</b>

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.110
<b>Kurata Kozue</b>

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:17.850
Hey! Aoyama!

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.240
Where are you going, Aoyama-kun?

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.060
Practice is about to start.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.700
<b>Aoyama Life</b>

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.700
Aoyama! You're not skipping 
practice, are you?!

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:38.740
Zaizen-san.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.890
Gramps! Bring the car round front!

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.330
Follow that bike—I mean, Aoyama!

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:50.310
We're bringing him back!

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.650
U-Um...

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:53.180
You get in, too!

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:58.510
Where is Aoyama-kun going?

00:09:58.510 --> 00:09:59.670
I don't know.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:02.080
<i>It's not like he's going home.</i>

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.200
<i>Oh, that's Ibuki's house.</i>

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.530
<i>So he's not going there either.</i>

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.710
<b>Oshigami-Minami High School</b>

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:19.260
What have we here? This is like the miracle 
of the young girl falling from the sky.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:24.100
So you've finally decided to join us, Aoyama?

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.100
You came again.

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:38.110
So that's what's going on? 
You sent the girl, Takechi!

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:39.410
Huh?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.480
Who are you?

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:44.120
Aoyama, I've lost all respect for you.
Falling for a woman's bait!

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:45.630
What are you blabbering about?

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:47.170
Don't play dumb with me!

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:48.580
Stop making a scene.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.290
Shut up!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.380
You're the problem here!

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.850
Hey, what's going on here?

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.800
Uh... Well, um, this is...

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.460
What? Do you want to see my abs?

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.410
Hell no, you ab-obsessed freak!

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:01.640
Jeez, why can't you just 
come straight to the field?

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.580
Are you listening, Seigo?!

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.730
Why are you at Oshigami-Minami?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:14.570
I don't know why, but Ibuki 
will be playing for us now.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.690
Seriously?

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:17.140
Wait, Aoyama!

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:20.790
You'd better not be thinking about joining
Oshigami-Minami because Ibuki is here!

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.910
What? Really, Aoyama?

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.290
Stop doing that!

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:28.900
Ah, you see, I heard about
 this soba place near here...

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.940
I'm really picky about my soba.

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.940
<b>Soba Shop</b>

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:35.470
He came back because he missed 
Japanese food too much.

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:36.550
What?!

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:40.000
Kozue came back with me, but her cooking's...

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.550
If you have a complaint, spit it out already!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.570
A-Are you two going out?

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:48.100
We're just childhood friends!

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:54.560
<b>Soba Shop</b>

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:51.780
Here, try this soba stick.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:54.560
Th-Thank you very much.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:59.570
<b>Soba Shop</b>

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.570
Soba sticks are yummy.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:07.870
Ibuki-san...

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.300
I'd like to have a 1-on-1 match.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.830
After delicious soba, I get a cocky upstart?

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:21.260
Not the worst thing after a meal.

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.830
So these are soba sticks, huh?

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.360
Are they always like this?

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:34.350
Yup, they always start a match.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:37.900
They get along because they were 
on the national team together.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.650
I was there, too!

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.460
Takechi-san, please stop them!

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:46.430
No, let's have them play.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:52.280
If it goes well, we might be able to get 
Aoyama to join Oshigami-Minami as well.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:58.250
If that happens, it'll be Takechi, Aoyama 
and Ibuki forming a colossal front line.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.620
The double crowns of summer and winter 
nationals won't just be a dream, then!

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.630
Don't come crying if you get in trouble
for doing this 'cause Coach isn't here.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.380
Aoyama-kun will win, right?

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:12.640
Yeah, I can't imagine Aoyama ever 
losing to another high-school player.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.140
First to three.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:19.330
If you lose, you know my terms.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.300
For Seigo, Aoyama's easy prey.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:34.420
What?!

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:38.770
Aoyama got beat?

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:39.670
No way.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.410
Looks like I've got
tonight's dinner in the bag.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:50.420
Round 2!

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:57.560
Beef bowl, tempura bowl, or pork bowl?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.440
No matter which I go for, 
your seasoning is on point!

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:04.590
Terrible.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:05.440
Huh?

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:09.740
I've decided.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.450
Pork cutlet rice bowl!

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.530
Let's call it a day.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.370
Hey, now... It's over?

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:29.000
Seigo's really off today. 
Aoyama noticed it, too.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.910
That was him having an off day?!

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:35.380
Takechi-san, looks like you're going 
to lose your spot as the team's striker.

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:36.470
What?!

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:40.230
What are you doing?

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:47.240
<b>Concentration</b>

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:47.240
<b>Stamina</b>

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:47.240
<b>Power</b>

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:47.240
<b>Technique</b>

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:47.240
<b>Speed</b>

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:46.580
Ibuki Seigo is on another level. 
All of his abilities eclipse Aoyama's.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:47.240
Aoyama

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.240
Ibuki

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:50.570
<b>Technique</b>

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:53.240
<b>Speed</b>

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:53.240
<b>Concentration</b>

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:53.240
<b>Stamina</b>

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:53.240
<b>Power</b>

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:53.240
Zaizen

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.620
Incidentally, this is you.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:53.240
What did you say?! You wanna go?!

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:55.220
I've had enough of your crap!

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:56.240
Zaizen-san, please stop.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:57.300
Let me down!

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:57.840
Shut up!

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.250
<i>Aoyama-kun...</i>

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:07.740
Kozue!

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.310
Oh, it's you, Aoyama.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:14.760
I'm coming in.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.270
Sure.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:21.540
Did something happen?

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:27.980
So good! You really are 
a genius in the kitchen!

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.280
Seconds, please!

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:35.780
Please cheer up. There's no 
point in winning like that.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:40.610
Kozue?!

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:46.150
Takechi

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:45.540
Oh, it's Takechi.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:46.540
Nah.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:52.450
So Kurata Kozue's the reason for it?

00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:56.050
I put mayonnaise on it.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:16:00.190
Kozue's food is always lightly seasoned.

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.480
<i>Mayonnaise heaven!</i>

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:08.070
She found out.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:12.490
Why did you do that? Are you stupid?!

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:16.390
I put it on because I wanted 
to enjoy the meal my way!

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.240
Besides, it's because 
your cooking sucks!

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.260
So you were dumped.

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:32.720
Not dumped! She's just in a bad mood!

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:40.830
I can see everything in soccer so clearly,
but with girls, I have no freaking clue!

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.650
Please, Aoyama! Help me make up with Kozue!

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.360
All right.

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:49.790
Really?!

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:52.810
Call Kurata Kozue.

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:55.430
Huh? What for?

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:57.990
A date.

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:04.310
<i>Why does he want to go on 
a date all of a sudden?</i>

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:09.070
<i>And why did I dress up like this? 
Why am I getting my hopes up?</i>

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.630
Sorry, did you wait long?

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.130
N-Not really.

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:14.130
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.020
Hey.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:21.610
If Kurata Kozue is mad, you should 
go meet her while wearing this.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.730
Huh? That?

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.650
Why do you even have that?

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:32.250
Cats heal people. I'm sure 
this would also calm her anger.

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:38.410
<i>Rather than calm her, I feel 
like she's getting even angrier.</i>

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:40.900
I-Ibuki...

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:47.380
<i>Nutritional science, first-class recipes,</i>

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:51.150
<i>nutritional science for athletes,
food and nutrition...</i>

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:54.730
Kozue.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:56.020
Wh-What is it?

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:58.290
I'm sorry about the other day.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:00.480
It wasn't right,
after you'd put in all that effort.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:05.420
<i>Exactly. My cooking isn't lightly 
seasoned because I'm useless in the kitchen.</i>

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:10.440
<b>Nutritional Science 
for Athletes</b>

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:10.440
<b>First 
Class
Recipes</b>

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.860
<i>It's because I carefully 
calculate nutritional values,</i>

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:10.440
<i>keeping Seigo's health and future in mind!</i>

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:13.180
<i>If he puts mayo on it, 
all those calculations go to waste!</i>

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:20.950
This isn't much, but here...

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.700
<i>Seigo got me a present?</i>

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.420
<i>Does this mean he understands what I'm doing?</i>

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.480
Can I open it?

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:30.850
S-Sure.

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:34.910
A present?

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:35.850
Yes.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:39.570
You're a genius! And what should I get her?

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:41.470
Let's see...

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:46.980
<b>Introduction 
to Cooking</b>

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:46.980
<b>You can do it even if you're not good!!</b>

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:46.050
What's this supposed to be?

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.380
Even if you're not good, if you put 
in the effort, you can improve.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.480
I don't need this! Are you mocking me?!

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.700
It's a good book, though.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:55.510
Ow!

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:56.610
Ow!

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:04.090
Hey, Aoyama, I feel like Kozue is
getting angrier by the minute.

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:06.120
Let's move on to the next phase.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.120
<b>Futsal 
Court</b>

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:11.370
A futsal court?

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:14.510
You go change, too.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.130
Wait a second...

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:19.630
Let's go, Kozue!

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:23.060
As if I could ever beat you at soccer!

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.220
It's futsal.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.110
It's the same!

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:29.020
<i>Playing together brings you closer.
That's the power of sport.</i>

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:33.020
You soccer-obsessed idiot! 
I've had it with you!

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:37.610
<i>Why do you think I went to Spain with you?!</i>

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:43.110
<i>Why do you think I was making you 
lightly seasoned food?!</i>

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:48.120
<i>Why do you think I came to 
the same school as you?!</i>

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:52.870
<i>It's all because I love you,</i>

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:57.380
<i>because I love the way you love soccer.</i>

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:02.380
<i>And because I wanted to 
try to help you with that!</i>

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.490
<i>Why can't you...</i>

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:10.140
<i>understand that?!</i>

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:16.710
Huh?

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:21.770
It looks like you two are 
feeling a bit better again.

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:25.420
This guy.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.820
<i>It always ends up like this.</i>

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:33.670
<i>I knew this all along.</i>

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:37.670
<i>Seigo doesn't understand me at all.</i>

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:41.170
<i>He'll probably never change.</i>

00:20:41.810 --> 00:20:44.180
All right! I win!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.210
You've got a long way to go!

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:50.420
Seigo.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:56.190
I brought some food. 
If you want, you can eat it.

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.060
Just so you know, the seasoning is—

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:00.860
So good!

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.950
Kozue, this is good!

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:10.010
Seigo, I'm sorry I got mad.

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:12.950
Huh? What's gotten into you now?

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:17.870
Well, you're eating my food
so enthusiastically...

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:21.980
You know how it is...

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:25.970
When you're hungry, everything tastes good!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.390
You jerk!

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.410
What now? I don't get you!

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:34.880
I'm so breaking up with you!

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.570
Hey, where are you going?

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:38.790
Kozue? Kozue-chan?!

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:40.480
I'll win next time.

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:46.790
<i>It's not just his house. Everything 
about Aoyama is a mystery.</i>

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:36.540
Sa-ka-i! Sa-ka-i!

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:30.510
Huh?

00:23:35.210 --> 00:23:36.290
I can hear them.

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Sakai-kun's Hairstyle Has Changed</b>
